after you install laravel/installer on ubuntu or any other distro you should add it to the path like this 


first check if laravel is actually installed 
  $ composer global list | grep laravel

then find composer global path
  $ composer global config bin-dir --absolute

 and then you can finally add it to path like this 

  # $HOME should work but if it didn't replace it with composer full path like this /home/username/.config/composer/vendor/bin
 $ echo 'export PATH="$PATH:$HOME/.composer/vendor/bin"' >> ~/.bashrc
 $ source ~/.bashrc
